# UI component consistency (workoutlogger / Logbook)

When adding or changing UI in `src/`, **reuse existing components and style helpers** instead of new one-off markup. Before writing JSX, search the codebase for an existing pattern in the same feature area (food, lifelog, workout, bike, dashboard) and match it.

## Page shell

| Need | Use | Do not |
|------|-----|--------|
| App page with nav | `Layout` from `@/components/Layout` | Custom full-page wrappers |
| Standard page width / padding | `PageContainer`, `narrowMobileWideDesktopClass`, `homePageShellClass` from `@/components/layout/PageContainer` | Ad-hoc `max-w-* mx-auto px-*` on every page |
| Sticky page title bar inside `PageContainer` | `pageStickyHeaderClass`, `pageTitleClass`, `pageSubtitleClass` from `@/lib/pageChrome` | Mixed `-mx-4` without `lg:-mx-8`, `bg-iron-950/95` vs `bg-slate-50/95` |
| Sheet layout-only overrides on `ModalContent` | `modalSheetLayoutClass` from `@/lib/pageChrome` (surface comes from `ui/modal`) | Per-screen `bg-iron-900 border-iron-800` on sheets |
| List / section enter animation | `FadeIn`, `SpringIn`, `StaggerContainer`, `StaggerItem`, `PressableScale` from `@/components/ui/fade-in` | Custom CSS animations unless matching an existing screen |

## Section chrome

| Need | Use | Do not |
|------|-----|--------|
| Icon + title + optional meta + right actions | `SectionHeader`, `SectionHeaderLink` from `@/components/SectionHeader` | Raw `<h2>`/`<h3>` + flex rows with duplicate typography |
| Habits / food / today card outer wrapper | `SectionSurface` / `sectionSurfaceClass` from `@/components/SectionSurface` | Copy-pasted `rounded-card border p-4` combinations |
| Empty list / no data (with optional CTA) | `EmptyState`, `EmptyInline` from `@/components/EmptyState` | Custom bordered boxes with “No items” text |
| Loading placeholders | `SkeletonLoader` exports (`SkeletonList`, `SkeletonSection`, etc.) from `@/components/SkeletonLoader` | Inline gray pulse divs |

## Overlays: pick exactly one primitive

**Default for mobile-first forms, pickers, and “sheets”:** bottom drawer via `@/components/ui/modal` (`Modal`, `ModalContent`, `ModalHeader`, `ModalTitle`, `ModalBody`, `ModalFooter`, `NestedModal`). This is the app standard (vaul).

| Scenario | Component |
|----------|-----------|
| Form sheet, food picker, settings panel, add/edit flows | `@/components/ui/modal` |
| Multi-field sheet with shared save/cancel layout | `@/components/ui/SheetFormLayout` |
| Top-left actions on a sheet (Save, Done, Delete) | `sheetTopActionButtonClass` / `sheetTopActionDestructiveClass` from `@/components/ui/sheetTopActions` |
| Dismiss a sheet | `ModalContent` ✕ (`showCloseButton`, default on) only — **no separate Cancel** pill when ✕ is shown |
| Small **centered** modal (export, compact picker, desktop-friendly dialog) | `@/components/ui/dialog` — only when centered UI is intentional; follow `RoutineDayPickerDialog`, `WorkoutExportModal` |
| Destructive or irreversible confirm | `@/components/ui/alert-dialog` |
| Long-press / row overflow menu | `@/components/ui/context-menu` |
| Tabs in a section | `@/components/ui/tabs` |

**Do not:**

- Mix `dialog` and `modal` for the same interaction type on the same surface (e.g. food add on one page as sheet, another as centered dialog).
- Duplicate modal header/footer markup; use `ModalHeader` / `ModalFooter` or `SheetFormLayout`.

## Buttons and actions

Use `@/lib/actionButtonStyles` (and existing size helpers in the same file if present):

- **One primary CTA per screen:** `actionPrimary(isDarkMode, …)`
- **Secondary:** `actionSecondary` / `actionSecondaryCompact`
- **Ghost / text:** `actionGhost`
- **Delete / discard confirm:** `actionDestructive`

Pair with `hapticLight` / `hapticMedium` from `@/lib/touchFeedback` where sibling screens already do.

**Do not** invent new red/green button class strings when an `action*` helper exists.

## Pickers and pending UI

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Emoji | `@/components/ui/emoji-picker` |
| Color | `@/components/ui/color-picker` |
| Async / placeholder media | `PendingIcon`, `PendingPlaceOverlay` from `@/components/ui/` |

## Charts

Dashboard and macro charts should use:

- `ChartBody`, `ChartSection`, `ChartSectionHeader` from `@/components/charts/ChartChrome`
- `RichChartTooltip` from `@/components/charts/RichChartTooltip`
- `ChartInsightFooter` when other charts in the same area use it

Heavy chart bundles: prefer existing `lazyCharts` / feature `lazy*` imports.

## Domain components (prefer over rebuilding)

- Workout session UI: `src/components/workout/*` (e.g. `SessionAddExerciseSheet`, `ReorderableExerciseTileGrid`, `workoutToolbarChrome`)
- Macros / food: `src/components/macros/*`, `FoodQuantityModal`, domain modals under `macros/`
- Life log / habits: `src/components/lifelog/*`, `LifeLogEventQuickGlyph`, `HabitPills`
- Bike: `src/components/bike/*`
- Planner: `src/components/planner/*`
- Exercise library / media: `src/components/exercises/*`

If two screens need the same UI, **extract or extend** the existing component; do not fork a second copy in a page file.

## Styling

- Use design tokens: `surface-*`, `text-section-header`, `text-metadata`, `rounded-card`, `border-surface-subtle`, not raw `slate-*` / `gray-*` unless matching legacy code you are not touching.
- Use `cn` from `@/lib/utils` for class merging.
- Icons: `lucide-react` — import every icon you use in JSX (production build fails on missing imports).

## Workflow when fixing inconsistency

1. Identify the **canonical screen** (newest or most polished) for that interaction type.
2. Replace ad-hoc markup with the shared component from the tables above.
3. If the canonical pattern is wrong but used in 3+ places, refactor the shared component once instead of adding a fourth variant.
4. Run `npm run verify` after substantive `src/` changes.

## Anti-patterns (reject in review)

- New `<div className="rounded-xl border ...">` section cards when `SectionSurface` / `EmptyState` fits
- Inline `<h3 className="text-sm font-semibold">` section titles when `SectionHeader` fits
- Raw `<button className="bg-red-600">` for delete when `actionDestructive` fits
- `Dialog` for a full-height mobile form that elsewhere uses `Modal`
- Page-level 200-line modal markup that should be `SheetFormLayout` or a named component under `src/components/`
